'' Assignment is a different question from promotion and the answers do not follow
'' from each other: 'long + string' and 'long = string' are both refused, but every
'' numeric-to-numeric assignment is accepted -- narrowing and all -- without so much
'' as a warning. The pointer rules are the interesting part: a pointer converts to and
'' from an integer of POINTER WIDTH with a warning and to nothing narrower, and two
'' different concrete pointees warn while ANY PTR is silent.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --check tests/types/src/assign.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: 12 assign:ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 17 assign:ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 19 assign:warn
'' EXPECT-OUT: 20 assign:warn
'' EXPECT-OUT: 21 assign:warn
'' EXPECT-OUT: 22 assign:reject
'' EXPECT-OUT: 23 assign:reject
'' EXPECT-OUT: 24 assign:reject
